; Floor features: a recess carved into a floor block — the wall-niche idea laid
; flat. The mesh builder stamps the feature's tile IN PLACE OF the cell's floor
; block, into the same variant bucket, so it wears whatever floor texture that
; cell wears. That is the whole point: a hole in the floor that is actually part
; of the floor, rather than a prop parked on top of one.
;
; A feature mesh must span the full cell (x,z in [-0.5, 0.5]) with its surface at
; y = 0 and use the floor block's UVs (u = x + 0.5, v = z + 0.5), or the cell
; stops tiling with its neighbours. tools/BuildFloorRecess.py is the reference,
; and asserts both.
;
; `texture` is deliberately absent — the cell supplies it.

[recess]
display = Floor Recess
model = floor_recess
